WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:03.595
Mind Your Decisions. I am Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.035 --> 00:00:07.045
In a rectangle, two line segments are drawn

00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:10.325
dividing the rectangle into four regions.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.320
Three of the regions have areas of 1, 3 and 4.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.180
What is the area of the 4th region?

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.140
The diagram is not drawn to scale.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.680
Pause the video if you like to give this problem a try,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.440
and when you are ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.860
We get started by focusing on these two triangles.

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:43.655
These two angles are equal to each other

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.360
because of vertical angles.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.220
Next, these two angles are equal to each other

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.720
because of alternate interior angles.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.780
This is because opposite sides of rectangle are parallel to each other.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.060
Consequently, these two triangles have two equal angles,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.440
which means all three angles are equal and these triangles are similar.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.180
As the areas are in ratio of 4:1,

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.620
their sides would in a ratio of 2:1.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.700
That's because the area is proportional to side length squared.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.080
Suppose the top triangle has a side length of a,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.300
its corresponding side length in the bottom triangle must be 2a.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.705
If the top triangle has a height of h,

00:01:25.705 --> 00:01:28.755
then the bottom triangle would has a height of 2a.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.100
Consider the area of the top triangle,

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.240
it would be a times h all over 2,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.940
that would be equal to 1.

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:40.015
This means ah is equal to 2.

00:01:41.095 --> 00:01:43.405
Now go back to the rectangle.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.160
We can solve for one of its side length.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.905
It would be equal to h plus 2h.

00:01:49.905 --> 00:01:52.245
Therefore, this side length would be 3h.

00:01:52.675 --> 00:01:54.665
The other side length is 2a.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:59.025
Therefore, the area of this entire rectangle

00:01:59.025 --> 00:02:01.575
would be 2a multiplies by 3h,

00:02:01.635 --> 00:02:04.625
which is equal to 6ah.

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:08.460
Since ah is equal to 2, 6ah would be equal to 12.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.040
We can then solve the problem quite easily.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.560
Three of the areas in the rectangle are 1, 3 and 4,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.935
that means the last area would be 12 minus 1 minus 3 minus 4,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.820
and that's equal to 4,

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.900
and that's the missing area.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.680
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.600
As always, thanks for watching. Thanks for your support.

